WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.624 --> 00:00:06.005
(electro music)

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.958
- My mother swore to her dying days

00:00:08.958 --> 00:00:12.278
that my first words were mama,
dada, resistor, capacitor.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.361
(laughs)

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:17.507
I don't know if they had geeks back then

00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:20.186
but I was probably one of them.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:23.076
(electro music)

00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:25.699
There is a resurgence,
the 20- and 30-somethings

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:29.056
have discovered analog
audio and they like it.

00:00:29.056 --> 00:00:30.563
(electro music)

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:34.282
There is no question that
cassettes are making a comeback.

00:00:34.282 --> 00:00:36.949
(electro music)

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.667
We are in the last cassette
factory in the United States.

00:00:44.185 --> 00:00:47.346
This company duplicates audio cassettes

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:50.013
and loads blank audio cassettes.

00:00:51.754 --> 00:00:53.521
We're like a printing press.

00:00:53.521 --> 00:00:56.960
They send us the audio,
graphics that they want,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.302
they specify if they want it in a box

00:00:59.302 --> 00:01:01.552
and we put it all together.

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:08.898
National Audio Company has been
around since about 1968, 69.

00:01:08.898 --> 00:01:10.562
(plastic clinks)

00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:13.320
When we first got into duplicating

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.496
it was mostly small runs,
the occasional band,

00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:19.553
some special order things.

00:01:19.553 --> 00:01:22.803
And then, about four or five years ago,

00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:26.334
there was a sudden change.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:29.404
(increasing electronic note)

00:01:29.404 --> 00:01:32.154
Every garage band you can imagine

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.967
showed up at our doorstep
wanting cassettes.

00:01:38.262 --> 00:01:41.280
2015 was probably our biggest year

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.192
and this year is without question

00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:46.581
on target for exceeding it.

00:01:46.581 --> 00:01:49.908
(electro music)

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:52.491
Analog brings a sense of warmth

00:01:53.764 --> 00:01:56.216
that is not present in digital.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.883
(electro music)

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.918
The download is so
temporary and so passing.

00:02:03.918 --> 00:02:06.591
You know, it's there and, it’s
okay, you listen to it

00:02:06.591 --> 00:02:08.501
and you enjoy it, but you have

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.483
nothing to go back and look at.

00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:13.463
The fact of holding it in your hand

00:02:13.463 --> 00:02:18.392
seems to be one of the
drawing cards for the cassette,

00:02:18.392 --> 00:02:21.822
and then for the older people
would be the nostalgia thing.

00:02:21.822 --> 00:02:24.489
(electro music)

00:02:26.351 --> 00:02:31.127
I think the cassettes have
made a permanent return.

00:02:31.127 --> 00:02:33.732
Shouldn't have gone
away in the first place.

00:02:33.732 --> 00:02:36.197
But they did, and now they're back.

00:02:36.197 --> 00:02:38.461
(electro music)

00:02:38.461 --> 00:02:42.577
My biggest concern is to pass
this on to somebody else.

00:02:42.577 --> 00:02:45.873
Yes, there's other people
that know how to do this,

00:02:45.873 --> 00:02:47.677
most of them are my age.

00:02:47.677 --> 00:02:51.344
So I need to teach and
train younger people.

00:02:53.094 --> 00:02:57.519
I wanna see National
Audio continue for as long

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:00.019
as there are tapes to be made.

